 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "s0",
   "title": "The goal",
   "text": "In stroke \\(a\\to b\\) the gas expands at constant temperature \\(T_1\\) from \\(V_1\\) to \\(V_2\\). The work done by the gas is \\(W=\\int P\\,dV\\), the **area under the curve**. Let us find that area exactly.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "N": 0
     },
     "at": 0
    }
   ],
   "dwell": 5200
  },
  {
   "id": "s1",
   "title": "Cut the area into strips",
   "text": "Slice the area into thin vertical strips. Each strip is almost a rectangle of height \\(P\\) and width \\(\\Delta V\\), so its area is \\(P\\,\\Delta V\\). Adding all of them gives \\(W\\approx\\sum P\\,\\Delta V\\). Here: **6** strips.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "N": 6
     },
     "at": 0
    }
   ],
   "dwell": 5600
  },
  {
   "id": "s2",
   "title": "Thinner strips fit better",
   "text": "Make the strips thinner and thinner. The steps melt into the curve and the sum becomes the integral \\(W=\\int_{V_1}^{V_2}P\\,dV\\). Drag **Number of strips** to see it.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "tween": {
      "N": 60
     },
     "at": 0,
     "dur": 3200
    }
   ],
   "dwell": 5600
  },
  {
   "id": "s3",
   "title": "Put in P = nRT/V",
   "text": "For an ideal gas \\(PV=nRT\\), so \\(P=nRT_1/V\\). The temperature is constant on an isotherm, so \\(nRT_1\\) is a constant and comes **outside** the integral: \\(W=nRT_1\\int dV/V\\).",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "N": 60
     },
     "at": 0
    }
   ],
   "dwell": 6000
  },
  {
   "id": "s4",
   "title": "Do the integral",
   "text": "Calculus: \\(\\int dV/V=\\ln V\\). Put in the limits: \\(W=nRT_1(\\ln V_2-\\ln V_1)=nRT_1\\ln\\dfrac{V_2}{V_1}\\).",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "N": 60
     },
     "at": 0
    }
   ],
   "dwell": 6000
  },
  {
   "id": "s5",
   "title": "Heat absorbed",
   "text": "The temperature is constant, so \\(\\Delta U=0\\) and the first law gives \\(Q=W\\). Hence \\(Q_1=W_{ab}=nRT_1\\ln\\dfrac{V_2}{V_1}\\). For 1 mol at \\(T_1={{T1|0}}\\) K and \\(V_2/V_1={{Vr|1}}\\): \\(Q_1={{Wex|0}}\\) J.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "N": 60
     },
     "at": 0
    }
   ],
   "dwell": 6000
  }
 ],
